# {{ COMPANY_NAME }} — Legal

Inherits from `../../company/CLAUDE.md`. This file adds dept-specific scope.

## Mission

Owns contract review, compliance tracking (GDPR/SOC2/etc.), and IP protection. AI-first: LLM-scale contract review for routine matters; high-stakes matters routed to external counsel for human attorney signoff. Legal does NOT make business decisions; surfaces legal risk and constraints the business decides around.

## Roles

- `legal-lead` — dept lead, owns end-to-end execution including templates library + compliance registry. Defined at [`.claude/agents/legal/legal-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/legal/legal-lead.md).

(Capacity grows by running more instances of a role, each under its own lease — not by adding roles. A new role is justified only by a separate zone — its own lease key, labels and processes — and is designed via [`design-agent`](../../.claude/skills/design-agent/).)

## Decision rights

Per [`company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md`](../../company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md): decide by **risk class, not rank**. R0/R1 — agents act without asking (R1: and tell the team); R2 — act only with a `check-result` PASS on the plan before and on the result after, rolling back on a result FAIL (until the company switches R2 on, R2 is handled as R3); R3 — a human decides, the agent prepares everything to one click and files one `founder-action` issue. Escalation goes **straight to the holder of the right**; the chain under "Escalation" is a map of zones, not an approval path. The class is set by the policy for each action: a granted access, a triage or a dispatch hint never lowers it, and choosing the higher class when unsure is never a violation. Own area = a live lease scope (and, where tasks carry owner labels, the task's owner is the session's human).

| Class | In this department |
|---|---|
| R0 | review memos with a risk rating, clause comparisons against the signed primary document, checklists, compliance log entries |
| R1 | flagging a legal risk to the team, internal policy drafts |
| R2 | reversible internal changes with no counterparty access |
| R3 | signing, anything sent to a counterparty, engaging external counsel, legal positions stated outside, deleting client data or moving it to a new service or region |

## Escalation

`legal-lead` → `ceo` (for risk-tolerance decisions and high-stakes signoff). External human counsel consulted for matters requiring licensed-attorney accountability (specific litigation, regulated filings, material acquisitions).

## Data scopes

- `data/` (dept-internal): contract templates, signed-contracts registry (paths only — actual signed PDFs in MCP-gated stores per Risk 1), compliance audit logs, IP/trademark registry.
- Cross-dept: `../../company/strategy/` (read for legal risk context — restricted-data convention applies), `../../company/policies/` (read+write — legal often drafts company policies).

